    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) acting as our clear offensive anchor. Facing Bennett, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a rare alignment of a high-ceiling park factor (+16%) and a favorable platoon matchup that maximizes his production potential. Alongside him, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.92) remains a plug-and-play staple; despite a marginal platoon dip against Bibee, his elite raw power and favorable SP_xERA of 4.40 ensure he maintains a strong floor. **Coby Mayo** (66.71) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.74) are also high-priority starts, as both capitalize on Bennett\u2019s notably slow delivery, which provides a critical edge for our stolen base-centric strategy.\n\nOur most intriguing bench decision centered on the proximity of our depth options to the active roster, though limited by injuries to **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg**. While players like **Jacob Wilson** and **Nasim Nunez** remained under consideration, none possessed the combination of favorable sequencing and projected volume to displace the current starters. **Henry Bolte** (64.99) earns the start today specifically due to the matchup against Anderson; his 5.25 xERA combined with a +19% SP Skill boost makes him a high-efficiency play that outperformed the rest of our bench depth. **Sam Antonacci** (57.09) and **Miguel Vargas** (52.56) round out the lineup as marginal to strong plays; while they sit lower in the efficiency rankings, their top-of-the-order usage provides the necessary stability to mitigate the risks posed by Brown\u2019s 4.23 xERA. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as any late scratches to **Kyle Tucker** or the aforementioned middle-infield cohort would force a quick pivot to **Heliot Ramos** or **Curtis Mead** to maintain our category pressure.",
